GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pages/builds/{build_id}
Gets information about a GitHub Pages build. OAuth app tokens and personal access tokens (classic) need the `repo` scope to use this endpoint.
Required: owner (path) — The account owner of the repository. The name is not case sensitive.; repo (path) — The name of the repository without the `.git` extension. The name is not case sensitive.; build_id (path)

GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pages/deployments/{pages_deployment_id}
Gets the current status of a GitHub Pages deployment. The authenticated user must have read permission for the GitHub Pages site.
Required: owner (path) — The account owner of the repository. The name is not case sensitive.; repo (path) — The name of the repository without the `.git` extension. The name is not case sensitive.; pages_deployment_id (path) — The ID of the Pages deployment. You can also give the commit SHA of the deployment.
